Package: pvstackr
Title: Stacked-Fit Calibration to Rubin/BRR-Fay Fixed-Effect Targets for Plausible Values
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R:
    person("JoonHo", "Lee", , "jlee296@ua.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-4019-8703"))
Description: Provides tools for Bayesian-backend fixed-effect calibration and
    reporting with plausible-value survey data. The package supports
    one-stacked-fit workflows for Bayesian backends while assembling external
    Rubin/BRR-Fay fixed-effect targets and calibrating fixed-effect draws to
    those targets.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://joonho112.github.io/pvstackr/,
    https://github.com/joonho112/pvstackr
BugReports: https://github.com/joonho112/pvstackr/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.3.0)
Suggests:
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    survey,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: Optional CmdStan and a C++ toolchain for live cmdstanr/brms
    workflows; sufficient memory for real PISA-scale data. These are not
    required for installation, loading, examples, or default tests.
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/testthat/parallel: false
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
